        "GET /library/chains/group?id=<nonexistent-uuid> returns HTTP 404",
        "The response HTML contains the group name",
        "The response HTML contains the group description when set",
        "No 404 when clicking a group item link (group_item.html href already points to this route)"
      ],
      "architectural_context": [
        "Page routes live in apps/webapp/src/webapp/api/pages/chains.py and are registered via api/pages/__init__.py",
        "Page templates use Jinja2 SSR, extend layouts/base.html, and are compiled from Astro .ts files in frontend/astro/src/pages/pages/",
        "The existing Astro fragment template dist/fragments/library/group_detail.html is already built — the new page template wraps it with {% extends 'layouts/base.html' %} and {% include 'fragments/library/group_detail.html' %}",
        "SignalChainGroupService.get_by_id() and SQLAlchemySignalChainGroupRepository exist and return the domain entity",
        "The fragment template expects: group.id, group.name, group.description, group.base_chain, group.permutation_count; also slots list with position, gear_count, gear_options (list with name), include_null",
        "The domain entity SignalChainGroup has slot_positions: list[int] and gear_options: dict[int, list[UUID]] and estimated_permutation_count() method"
      ],
      "navigation_hints": [
        "apps/webapp/src/webapp/api/pages/chains.py — add route after existing routes",
        "apps/webapp/src/webapp/services/signal_chain_group_service.py — SignalChainGroupService.get_by_id()",
        "frontend/astro/src/pages/fragments/library/group_detail.html.ts — existing fragment to include",
        "frontend/astro/src/pages/pages/library/chains.html.ts — model the new page .ts after this pattern",
        "frontend/astro/dist/pages/library/chains.html — model dist output after this file"
      ],
      "implementation_notes": [
        "Route signature: GET /library/chains/group with id: UUID = Query(...)",
        "The group entity has gear_options: dict[int, list[UUID]] — build slots list as: [{position: pos, gear_count: len(ids), gear_options: [{name: str(gid)} for gid in ids], include_null: group.include_null} for pos, ids in group.gear_options.items()]",
        "For base_chain, query SignalChain by group.base_chain_id to get its name; use 'N/A' if not found",
        "Add import for SignalChainGroupService at top of chains.py",
        "The Astro page template is a .ts file exporting a GET function returning a Response with the Jinja2 template string; see chains.html.ts for exact pattern",
        "After writing the Astro .ts source file, also write the compiled dist .html (they should be identical content-wise)",
        "The chains fragment in the group_detail shows 'api/signal-chain-groups/{{ group.id }}' — no backend changes needed for that, the API already exists"
      ],
