    {
      "story_id": "02-shootout-chain-ownership",
      "name": "Enforce chain ownership in shootout creation",
      "purpose": "Prevent a user from including signal chains owned by others in a new shootout — returns 404 instead of silently succeeding.",
      "agent": {
        "model": "sonnet",
        "skills": [
          "gts-testing"
        ],
        "tools": [
          "Read",
          "Edit",
          "Write",
          "Bash",
          "Glob",
          "Grep"
        ]
      },
      "scope": {
        "create": [
          "tests/integration/webapp/test_shootout_chain_ownership.py"
        ],
        "modify": [
          "apps/webapp/src/webapp/api/pages/shootouts.py"
        ]
      },
      "state_assumption": "cumulative",
      "acceptance_criteria": [
        "POST /shootout/create with a chain_id owned by a different user returns HTTP 404",
        "POST /shootout/create with chain_ids all owned by the current user succeeds and returns HX-Redirect",
        "The existing golden-path test suite continues to pass after this change"
      ],
      "architectural_context": [
        "shootout_create_submit is a page route (POST /shootout/create) in apps/webapp/src/webapp/api/pages/shootouts.py",
        "It currently reads chain_ids from form data and creates ShootoutChain value objects without verifying ownership",
        "Pattern: fetch each chain via SQLAlchemySignalChainRepository.get_by_id(), check chain.user_id == current_user.id, raise HTTPException(404) if not",
        "SQLAlchemySignalChainRepository is already imported locally inside shootout_create_chains_fragment — use same local import inside shootout_create_submit",
        "Resource ownership rule: return 404 not 403 to avoid leaking existence"
      ],
      "navigation_hints": [
        "apps/webapp/src/webapp/api/pages/shootouts.py:335 — shootout_create_submit function",
        "apps/webapp/src/webapp/adapters/persistence/repositories/signal_chain_repository.py — SQLAlchemySignalChainRepository.get_by_id()",
        "apps/webapp/src/webapp/api/pages/chains.py:193 — existing ownership check pattern: if not chain or chain.user_id != current_user.id"
      ],
      "implementation_notes": [
        "After collecting chain_ids and before building ShootoutChainVO list, add a validation loop",
        "For each chain_id in chain_ids: call repo.get_by_id(UUID(chain_id)), if not found or chain.user_id != current_user.id raise HTTPException(404, 'Chain not found')",
        "Import SQLAlchemySignalChainRepository locally inside the function (matching the pattern in shootout_create_chains_fragment)",
        "The ownership check must happen before creating ShootoutEntity — fail fast"
      ],
      "truths_addressed": [
        3,
        4
      ],
      "test_spec": {
        "test_type": "integration",
        "fixtures": [
          "make_user",
          "make_di_track",
          "make_signal_chain"
        ],
        "assertions": [
          {
            "type": "http_status",
            "details": {
              "method": "POST",
              "route": "/shootout/create",
              "auth": "test_user",
              "body": {
                "name": "Test",
                "di_track_id": "{di_track.id}",
                "chain_ids[]": [
                  "{other_user_chain.id}",
                  "{other_user_chain2.id}"
                ]
              },
              "expected_status": 404
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "http_status",
            "details": {
              "method": "POST",
              "route": "/shootout/create",
              "auth": "test_user",
              "body": {
                "name": "Test",
                "di_track_id": "{di_track.id}",
                "chain_ids[]": [
                  "{own_chain.id}",
                  "{own_chain2.id}"
                ]
              },
              "expected_status": 200
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "story_id": "03-comment-edit-api",
      "name": "PATCH /api/v1/comments endpoint for comment editing",
      "purpose": "Add the backend API endpoint, service method, and repository method for editing a comment body, with ownership enforced at 404.",
      "agent": {
        "model": "sonnet",
        "skills": [
          "gts-testing"
        ],
        "tools": [
          "Read",
          "Edit",
          "Write",
          "Bash",
          "Glob",
          "Grep"
        ]
      },
      "scope": {
        "create": [
          "apps/webapp/src/webapp/api/v1/comments.py",
          "tests/integration/webapp/test_comment_edit_api.py"
        ],
        "modify": [
          "apps/webapp/src/webapp/adapters/persistence/repositories/shootout_comment_repository.py",
          "apps/webapp/src/webapp/services/shootout_comment_service.py",
          "apps/webapp/src/webapp/api/v1/schemas/shootout_comment.py",
          "apps/webapp/src/webapp/main.py"
        ]
      },
      "state_assumption": "cumulative",
      "acceptance_criteria": [
        "PATCH /api/v1/comments/{id} by the comment author with {\"body\": \"new text\"} returns HTTP 200 with updated comment JSON",
        "The returned JSON includes the updated content field",
        "PATCH /api/v1/comments/{id} by a non-author returns HTTP 404",
        "PATCH /api/v1/comments/{nonexistent-id} returns HTTP 404",
        "Empty or whitespace-only body is rejected with HTTP 422"
      ],
      "architectural_context": [
        "New router file api/v1/comments.py with prefix /api/v1/comments; registered in main.py alongside other v1 routers",
        "Follows signal_chain_groups.py pattern: uses get_current_user_required and get_db_session from webapp.auth.dependencies",
        "Repository layer: add update(comment_id, content) method to ShootoutCommentRepository — SELECT + mutate + flush + refresh",
        "Service layer: add update(comment_id, user_id, body) to ShootoutCommentService — validate ownership (raise ValueError if wrong user), validate body not empty, call repo.update()",
        "Schema: add CommentUpdateRequest with body: str field; reuse CommentResponse for the response",
        "Ownership failure: service raises ValueError with 'not authorized'; router maps this to 404 (not 403)",
        "The comment model stores text in the 'content' column; the API request field is named 'body' per epic spec"
      ],
      "navigation_hints": [
        "apps/webapp/src/webapp/api/v1/signal_chain_groups.py — model the new router after this file",
        "apps/webapp/src/webapp/adapters/persistence/repositories/shootout_comment_repository.py — add update() method",
        "apps/webapp/src/webapp/services/shootout_comment_service.py — add update() method",
        "apps/webapp/src/webapp/api/v1/schemas/shootout_comment.py — add CommentUpdateRequest",
        "apps/webapp/src/webapp/main.py:16 — add comments import alongside other v1 imports; include router same as others",
        "apps/webapp/src/webapp/adapters/persistence/models/shootout_comment.py — ShootoutComment ORM model with 'content' column"
      ],
      "implementation_notes": [
        "Repository update method: SELECT comment by id with joinedload(user), mutate comment.content = new_content, flush, refresh with ['user'], return comment",
        "Service update method signature: async def update(self, comment_id: UUID, user_id: UUID, body: str) -> ShootoutComment",
        "Service validates: body.strip() not empty; comment exists; comment.user_id == user_id (return 404 on mismatch); then calls repo.update()",
        "Router: PATCH /{comment_id} — fetch via service.update(), on ValueError raise 404, return CommentResponse",
        "In main.py, add 'from webapp.api.v1 import comments' and 'app.include_router(comments.router)'",
        "The router prefix is /api/v1/comments — distinct from /api/shootouts pattern used by older endpoints"
      ],
      "truths_addressed": [
        5,
        6
      ],
      "test_spec": {
        "test_type": "integration",
        "fixtures": [
          "make_user",
          "make_di_track",
          "make_shootout"
        ],
        "assertions": [
          {
            "type": "api_response",
            "details": {
              "method": "PATCH",
              "route": "/api/v1/comments/{comment.id}",
              "auth": "comment_author",
              "body": {
                "body": "Updated text"
              },
              "expected_status": 200,
              "expected_json": {
                "content": "Updated text"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "http_status",
            "details": {
              "method": "PATCH",
              "route": "/api/v1/comments/{comment.id}",
              "auth": "other_user",
              "body": {
                "body": "Hacked text"
              },
              "expected_status": 404
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "http_status",
            "details": {
              "method": "PATCH",
              "route": "/api/v1/comments/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
              "auth": "test_user",
              "body": {
                "body": "text"
              },
              "expected_status": 404
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "story_id": "04-comment-edit-ui",
      "name": "Inline comment editing UI with Alpine.js and HTMX",
      "purpose": "Add an edit button to own comments in the shootout comments fragment; clicking it shows an inline form that PATCHes the API and updates the comment text in-place.",
      "agent": {
        "model": "sonnet",
        "skills": [
          "gts-frontend-dev"
        ],
        "tools": [
          "Read",
          "Edit",
          "Write",
          "Bash",
          "Glob",
          "Grep"
        ]
      },
      "scope": {
        "create": [
          "tests/integration/webapp/test_comment_edit_ui.py"
        ],
        "modify": [
          "frontend/astro/src/pages/fragments/shootouts/comments.html.ts",
          "frontend/astro/dist/fragments/shootouts/comments.html"
        ]
      },
      "state_assumption": "cumulative",
      "acceptance_criteria": [
        "The comments fragment renders an edit button (data-testid='comment-edit') only when comment.is_own is true",
        "Users who did not write the comment see no edit button",
        "Clicking the edit button switches the comment item to show an editable textarea pre-filled with the current comment text",
        "Submitting the edit form calls PATCH /api/v1/comments/<id> and updates the displayed text on success",
        "The cancel button restores the original view without changes",
        "All existing delete and post-comment functionality continues to work"
      ],
      "architectural_context": [
        "comments.html.ts is an Astro SSG file that outputs a Jinja2 fragment template to dist/fragments/shootouts/comments.html",
        "The fragment already passes comment.is_own and comment.id in context via comment_to_context()",
        "Edit state management uses Alpine.js x-data on each comment item: {editing: false, editText: '{{ comment.text }}'}",
        "Submitting the edit uses Alpine.js fetch() calling PATCH /api/v1/comments/{{ comment.id }} with JSON body {body: editText}",
        "On success (status 200), update the displayed text and set editing: false",
        "No new backend routes needed — story 03 already created the PATCH endpoint",
        "After editing Astro .ts source, also update the compiled dist .html to match"
      ],
      "navigation_hints": [
        "frontend/astro/src/pages/fragments/shootouts/comments.html.ts — the full fragment template source to modify",
        "frontend/astro/dist/fragments/shootouts/comments.html — compiled output to update",
        "apps/webapp/src/webapp/api/pages/context.py:229 — comment_to_context() already returns is_own flag",
        "frontend/astro/src/pages/fragments/library/group_detail.html.ts — example of Alpine.js fetch pattern with POST/DELETE"
      ],
      "implementation_notes": [
        "Wrap each comment item div with x-data='{editing: false, editText: \"{{ comment.text | e }}\", currentText: \"{{ comment.text | e }}\"}' Alpine state",
        "Add edit button next to delete button: show only {% if comment.is_own %}, data-testid='comment-edit', @click='editing = true'",
        "When editing=true: show a textarea (x-model='editText') and Save/Cancel buttons; hide the display text",
        "Save button: @click='fetch(\"/api/v1/comments/{{ comment.id }}\", {method:\"PATCH\", headers:{\"Content-Type\":\"application/json\"}, body: JSON.stringify({body: editText})}).then(r=>r.json()).then(d=>{currentText=d.content; editing=false})'",
        "Cancel button: @click='editText=currentText; editing=false'",
